      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "GROUSE MOUNTAIN (2) resumes for a new yard. Her first up run last campaign when beaten a nose at Caulfield Heath reads very well for this before she got over a bit more ground. She's not lacking for speed and this looks suitable. ETERNAL JOY (8) is racing well, a maiden winner two back at Ballarat Synthetic before another sound effort there. Still lightly raced and should take beating again.This suits nicely. RUBY AVENUE (6) has just been fair of late on heavy tracks but could improve here. BOLD PRINT (4) comes back a notch in grade. He's the best suited back to the 1000m and has the speed to lead, will take catching.",
